WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.859
Zero-shot forecasting

00:00:01.671 --> 00:00:02.319
wins

00:00:02.355 --> 00:00:03.663
but not everywhere

00:00:04.182 --> 00:00:05.891
Google's TimesFM 3

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:06.575
leads the public

00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:07.200
benchmarks

00:00:07.236 --> 00:00:08.545
but those benchmarks

00:00:08.357 --> 00:00:09.394
use old public

00:00:09.206 --> 00:00:10.266
data the model

00:00:10.102 --> 00:00:10.998
may already have

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:12.071
seen during training

00:00:12.598 --> 00:00:13.647
The author tested

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:14.225
it on data

00:00:14.037 --> 00:00:15.215
published after its

00:00:15.027 --> 00:00:15.699
release

00:00:15.794 --> 00:00:16.961
sealed forecasts

00:00:16.997 --> 00:00:18.270
and seven thousand

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:19.531
six hundred synthetic

00:00:19.343 --> 00:00:20.015
series

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.135
with the protocol

00:00:20.947 --> 00:00:21.984
frozen first

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:23.586
The model wins

00:00:23.457 --> 00:00:24.695
but not everywhere

00:00:24.589 --> 00:00:25.603
and its prediction

00:00:25.415 --> 00:00:26.511
intervals come out

00:00:26.323 --> 00:00:27.289
narrower than they

00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:28.056
claim to be

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:29.604
Full story on

00:00:29.415 --> 00:00:30.311
the dashboard
